30,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The earth-moving firms are worried about clay and slippage. Big digs are risky, but small-plant work is fine.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"People mostly stick to firm ground to reach the tram. Also, drainage is failing and the heat is intense.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minato,,"We have very few staff left, but we have volunteers for habitat work and youth sports.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Past work shows that water basins last, but paved surfaces fail quickly. Also, many new trees died from poor aftercare.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The habitat fund only pays for planting and water. Meanwhile, planted areas cost triple to maintain compared to hard surfaces.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the ground is slippy and people want firm paths, we should avoid massive excavations.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. We need something that respects the current flow of traffic and handles the heat.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the maintenance cost is so high for plants, maybe the volunteers can help offset that?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, only if the city actually manages the contracts. The eastern avenue trees died because of bad planning.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, volunteers are great, but the budget gap for planted ground is widening every year.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, you said basins last. Maybe a water-based plan is safer than a big paved plaza?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A plaza might just become a heat island, given the August readings I saw.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minato,,The sports volunteers are a strong resource. That could be a way to keep the park active.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Minako,,I agree that water management seems more durable than the city's recent paving efforts.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,But the habitat fund only covers the start. The long-term upkeep of wetlands could be a financial drain.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Kenji,,We should avoid anything that requires massive earth-moving in the center.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. We need a balance between user behavior and environmental reality.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want to make sure whoever is chosen has people to actually run it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Minako,,Let's see the candidates and decide based on these risks.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for the option that doesn't bankrupt the maintenance budget.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
