55,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wetland Restoration seems safest for the soil, but Sports Terraces might be too much digging.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Market Plaza ignores the heat and the tram-stop traffic. Woodland Walk might be too soft for the commuters.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Minato,,Sports Terraces fits our youth league volunteers perfectly. Wetland Restoration fits the habitat volunteers.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Minako,,Wetland Restoration aligns with the durable overflow basins I saw in the records.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Wetland Restoration is funded by the habitat fund, but the upkeep ledger makes me nervous.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, but the Market Plaza would require surfacing that Minako says fails quickly.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minato, the Sports Terraces might interfere with the tram-stop crossing patterns.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, that's true. Maybe the Wetland boardwalks would guide people better?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Minako,,The Woodland Walk risks the same death rate as the eastern avenue trees.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If the habitat fund covers the capital, the initial cost is low. But the annual spend is the problem.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm leaning toward Wetland Restoration. It avoids the clay slippage risks of heavy construction.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It addresses the drainage issues and the heat. I support it.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minato,,I can see the habitat volunteers taking the lead there. I'm in.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Minako,,It's the most sustainable choice based on the earlier programme's success.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If the others are certain, and the fund covers the start, I can accept it, provided we use volunteers.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Kenji,,It seems we have a consensus.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic holds.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy with this.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
